# Secrets, above everything else. .env holds the model API key and possibly
# the LDAP service account password; a copy of it baked into an image layer
# is a copy that travels to wherever the image goes, and `docker history`
# will show it. Configuration reaches the container through env_file at run
# time instead.
.env
.env.backup*
.env.*.bak
*.pem
certs/

# State. users.db holds password hashes, sessions and the audit trail;
# history/ holds every conversation. Both belong in a volume, not an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
glossary.md

# Not needed at run time, and copying them makes the image bigger and the
# build slower for no gain.
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
tests/
tools/
node_modules/

.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documentation and working notes. Useful in the repository, dead weight in
# a container.
*.md
!README.md
readiness.html
deploy/
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
